  "plain": "In the 1970s, while in Washington to do research at the National Archives, the writer Peter Levenda says he walked into his hotel room near Dupont Circle and found that someone had left a huge poster on the wall of the eye in the pyramid, the symbol linked to the Illuminati, a secret society of legend. He tells Michels this from his own memory, as a moment that felt like more than chance."
